                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Played On: [b]HTC Vive[/b][/h1]\n\nPenrose Studios is the publisher/creator responsible for the 20 minute short film Allumette; a somewhat stop-motion animation inspired event. Preceeding that release is The Rose and I, another short release that takes on a lot of the same animation qualities as the aforementioned title. However, The Rose and I only lasts for about five minutes, and the story isn't very well crafted. There are some planets that zoom around, and you watch a little guy water a flower and then he sits down to gaze at the sunset. Honestly, that's it. If you're really down to experience all VR has to offer, at least this title is free. Otherwise, it's really not worth spending any time on, and you're better off giving Allumette or Google Spotlight Stories: Son of Jaguar a try instead.\n\n[h1]Rating: [b]2.5/5.0[/b] It's not bad, but it's not great.[/h1]\nThe VR Network [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/33182845-The-VR-Network/]Curator[/url] | [url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/thevrnetwork]Group[/url] Click for More",
